he superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the products of the known solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79770/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b6aed976-74f4-52eb-883e-d874f2e5b4a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c12f1c6a-7897-5050-955e-c30d6cb6868e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3783d887-6dde-593d-9216-b4737ee03743" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ec152012-bf24-54f6-912c-92eb68bc4fc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "72db357b-5e94-521b-98cb-2e27bb3c0ab9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d27e28cc-8bfa-530d-8835-f467eec06e85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-131016/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-131016/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-131016/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-131016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131016/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131016" :question/id #uuid "67dbd2c9-c2b1-519d-a98b-db897636de6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131016" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ are solutions to the equation $4{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\n- $y(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- $y(x)=\\sqrt{x}(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)$\n- $y(x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the products of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\sqrt{x}(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$  is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle because $\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is not one of the known solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131016/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131016"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0ab4bee3-410b-5d35-a169-2ad76e41fb2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d141c907-baeb-56b6-a4dc-73c8aaa2f339" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "0123dcd1-151b-5e93-b33c-8455ee006a17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7f88787e-12af-5ad0-bd43-09116993b631" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0649ef2a-c509-51a3-90f0-709555e3334a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5047de-6ecd-5229-ad34-95182ad33319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131019/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-131019/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-131019/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131019/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-131019/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-131019/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131019" :question/id #uuid "00e825fa-5929-5a6d-9ff6-6f8f75d69f5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131019" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear, second-order ODE, then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\n- $y(x)=x$\n- $y(x)=x{e}^{2x}$ $$\n- $y(x)=(1+x){e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=x=\\frac{x{e}^{x}}{{e}^{x}}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotients of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=x{e}^{2x}=x{e}^{x}({e}^{x})$  is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.  The superposition principle does not extend to the product of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=(1+x){e}^{x}={e}^{x}+x{e}^{x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131019/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79833/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "75a487b3-e8fe-54ab-aea5-9ccb506cab1e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79833/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f