}^{3-6x}$\n- $y(x)=-{e}^{6x}$" :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the function ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and $c$ is a constant, then $y(x)=c{y}_{1}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=2{e}^{-6x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=2.$\n\n- The function $y(x)={e}^{3-6x}={e}^{3}\\cdot {e}^{-6x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c={e}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $y(x)=-{e}^{6x}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle because $y={e}^{6x}$ is not a solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79833/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0829d4a-239a-5a8e-9c8e-3cdc76a993bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79774/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "bec5a050-34cd-58d0-8449-b9dcabaf82d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79774/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "07c8c2b6-a5e7-53a5-adb2-79404773427d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79774/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "aaae9815-b868-5a77-aee5-79142c179d66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79774/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b5209a10-aa98-53b5-895d-ecce39b09eae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:an