rposition principle. In this case, $c=2.$\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{x}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79774/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0829d4a-239a-5a8e-9c8e-3cdc76a993bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79832/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "79c5ffc1-f12f-5e0f-a0b8-1b58d24ccc54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79832/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cbddd149-3077-5012-84bf-e1799524c4bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79832/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c0e1aa36-60bc-59d8-b000-51261b8c6349" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79832/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "07338c9a-efd0-59bb-a0ad-c7ffc2db516f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79832/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "fa9e8daf-3b95-5a60-bdb0-85d9e86ba4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79832/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "838633f3-25f7-5014-8095-87e91b2aac41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79832/sele